      "id": 230265,
      "name": "flamethrower49",
      "username": "flamethrower49",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/f/838e76/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2020-04-15T05:52:38.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Mint at 3-1-1-0/6/0/9. Mainstay and KNYFE were down. An exceedingly quick and brutal game, ending on Bunker's third turn. Plague Rat does most of the work, especially with Writhe's significant help. Definitely try to think through the order of the Rat's attacks, especially turn one. Kill Order was Anvil (Bastion), then Greazer (when Plague Rat got KNYFE), then Anvil again and the Rat (second Blackout), then Hammer and Friction with some fancy modulating from Bunker.</p>\n<p>I did not make use of Wrecking Bastion or Infiltrating Twist the Ether, but both of those seem like they would go a long way towards an easier victory.</p>",
